02:53:32.100 --> 02:53:35.440
And she carries the scars or the marks of three different tests

02:53:35.440 --> 02:53:38.420
commonly used for testing cosmetics, ingredients and products.

02:53:38.750 --> 02:53:42.930
The rabbit's costume was designed by makers of the TV show Spitting Image.

02:53:43.170 --> 02:53:46.850
The hope is politicians in Europe will ban the use of any animal

02:53:46.850 --> 02:53:49.270
in tests for toiletries and cosmetics.

02:53:49.990 --> 02:53:52.030
We're now on to this afternoon's sports news

02:53:52.030 --> 02:53:54.590
and we start for the last time this season with football.

02:53:55.030 --> 02:53:57.010
Notts County's players have set off for Wembley

02:53:57.010 --> 02:53:59.970
for their promotion play-off final against Brighton tomorrow.

02:54:00.000 --> 02:54:03.200
For the winners, the prize is a place in the 1st Division.

02:54:04.710 --> 02:54:09.850
Final training session and a fairly relaxed atmosphere at Meadow Lane at lunchtime today

02:54:09.850 --> 02:54:16.410
as the Notts County squad prepared for the journey south and an overnight stop for tomorrow afternoon's Wembley date

02:54:16.410 --> 02:54:19.480
with Brighton in the 2nd Division promotion playoff.

02:54:20.290 --> 02:54:24.730
It's the most important game that all our lads, my lads and myself have played obviously

02:54:24.730 --> 02:54:28.530
and it's a league game to us although I know it's an occasion to everybody else

02:54:28.530 --> 02:54:29.970
but I've just told the lads that from now on.

02:54:30.000 --> 02:54:32.000
We're preparing for an important league match.

02:54:32.960 --> 02:54:36.520
The manager, who's likely to be back on Aston Villa's wanted list now,

02:54:36.700 --> 02:54:39.680
as well as being chased by Chelsea, travelled down alone.

02:54:39.920 --> 02:54:41.800
The rest of the squad went by coach.

02:54:42.200 --> 02:54:45.300
Last year, Notts won promotion to the second division via the playoffs.

02:54:45.680 --> 02:54:49.030
Now they hope to use the same route to make it to the first division.

02:54:50.070 --> 02:54:52.270
And exclusively on Central tomorrow evening,

02:54:52.390 --> 02:54:56.130
highlights of Notts County's playoff final with Brighton at Wembley Stadium.

02:54:56.900 --> 02:54:59.960
Now on to today's cricket, and the West Indies are playing their...

02:55:00.000 --> 02:55:05.140
final game before the first test with England next week. The Windies are at Leicester. Nigel

02:55:05.140 --> 02:55:13.030
Briers kept the Quicks at bay hitting 68 as Leicestershire moved on to 257 for five. There

02:55:13.030 --> 02:55:17.790
may be only five days to go before the first test but the West Indies still fielded a fairly

02:55:17.790 --> 02:55:23.230
strong side at Leicester but the county led by Nigel Briers weren't too keen on respecting

02:55:23.230 --> 02:55:29.140
reputations although Patrick Patterson working up a fair pace early on had Tim Boone caught behind.

02:55:31.050 --> 02:55:35.090
The prize, though, stayed put, and with Peter Hepworth and Laurie Potter

02:55:35.090 --> 02:55:38.370
both picking up half-centuries as well at a cold grace road,

02:55:38.550 --> 02:55:41.670
the West Indies have hardly had the preparation they'd have wanted

02:55:41.670 --> 02:55:43.480
for the Test Match series.

02:55:46.290 --> 02:55:49.310
Other cricket now, four wickets apiece for both Greg Thomas

02:55:49.310 --> 02:55:51.750
and his Northamptonshire teammate Kevin Curran,

02:55:51.910 --> 02:55:54.490
as Derbyshire were bowled out for 189.

02:55:54.850 --> 02:55:57.810
The Derbyshire player John Morris topscored with 87.

02:55:58.110 --> 02:55:59.970
Northampton were the first innings lead of 50.

02:56:00.000 --> 02:56:03.200
and they're now 39 without loss in their second innings.

02:56:03.960 --> 02:56:05.880
And at Trent Bridge, Franklin Stevenson

02:56:05.880 --> 02:56:07.640
picks up the early wicket of Chris Smith.

02:56:07.640 --> 02:56:13.240
Hampshire now 169 for three in reply to knots 189 all out.

02:56:14.100 --> 02:56:14.820
Now cycling.

02:56:15.040 --> 02:56:17.200
And the milk race is in the East Midlands today.

02:56:17.460 --> 02:56:19.720
Stage six of the Round Britain cycle race

02:56:19.720 --> 02:56:22.240
has brought the riders from Kettering to Leicester.

02:56:23.960 --> 02:56:26.540
Today's stage took the riders over 64 miles

02:56:26.540 --> 02:56:28.060
of Northamptonshire and Leicestershire

02:56:28.060 --> 02:56:29.920
before finishing in Leicester city centre.

02:56:30.220 --> 02:56:35.500
There was a 10-man breakaway 17 miles from home, but that was down to just two at the death.

02:56:35.920 --> 02:56:42.250
And the stage was won by the British amateur, Mark Gornall, just holding off Steve Deuce in the sprint finish.

02:56:44.520 --> 02:56:49.840
Chris Walker, though, is still the overall leader in the yellow jersey, 18 seconds clear of Simeon Hempsell.

02:56:50.240 --> 02:56:53.200
Tomorrow, stage seven of the milk race is around Birmingham.

02:56:54.440 --> 02:56:57.320
And that's it for tonight. Good luck to Notts County at Wembley tomorrow.

02:56:57.340 --> 02:56:59.360
Don't forget the highlights tomorrow night on Central.

02:57:00.000 --> 02:57:04.000
We're back with our next news bulletin at 5 to 1 tomorrow lunchtime.

02:57:04.140 --> 02:57:05.840
In the meantime, have a very good evening.

02:57:33.870 --> 02:57:38.720
Hello, it's been rather a cold start to June, and it looks like it's going to stay rather cold for the next week as well.

02:57:39.080 --> 02:57:42.400
And tonight, where clouds break, temperatures could get low enough for a touch of ground frost.

02:57:42.640 --> 02:57:45.100
Temperatures dipping close to 3, that's 37 Fahrenheit.

02:57:45.810 --> 02:57:49.030
Bright tomorrow morning with some sunshine, but it will cloud over during the afternoon,

02:57:49.210 --> 02:57:51.230
and there is the outside possibility of a shower.

02:57:51.540 --> 02:57:53.720
Temperatures only getting up to about 14, that's 57.

02:58:12.160 --> 02:58:14.880
Daytime Central. Make your day.

02:58:17.010 --> 02:58:25.140
In a couple of hours here on Central, Poirot has to look no further than the third floor flat in tonight's Agatha Christie mystery.

